### Portal Targeting
```typescript
import * as Dialog from '@radix-ui/react-dialog'

export function CustomPortal() {
  return (
    <Dialog.Root>
      <Dialog.Trigger>Open</Dialog.Trigger>
      {/* Render in specific container */}
      <Dialog.Portal container={document.getElementById('modal-root')}>
        <Dialog.Content>Content</Dialog.Content>
      </Dialog.Portal>
    </Dialog.Root>
  )
}
```

## Best Practices

1. **Use asChild for composition** - Merge Radix props with custom components
2. **Style with data attributes** - Use data-[state=...] for state-based styling
3. **Portal for overlays** - Always use Portal for dialogs, popovers, dropdowns
4. **Controlled state when needed** - Use open/onOpenChange for complex logic
5. **Tooltip.Provider** - Wrap app with Provider for consistent tooltip behavior
6. **Accessibility first** - Leverage built-in ARIA attributes and keyboard support
7. **Type safety** - Import types from @radix-ui/react-{component}
8. **CSS-in-JS or Tailwind** - Radix is unstyled, style however you prefer
9. **Test with keyboard** - Verify keyboard navigation works correctly
10. **Use Trigger asChild** - Avoid nested buttons by using asChild prop
11. **Single package import** - Use @radix-ui/react for all components
12. **Animation with CSS** - Use CSS transitions on data-[state] attributes
13. **Escape key handling** - Use onEscapeKeyDown for custom escape behavior
14. **Focus management** - Radix handles focus trapping automatically
15. **Combine with shadcn/ui** - Radix primitives work great with shadcn/ui
